# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/drafter-arms four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the integrated branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch that holds them.
# TWO IMAGES: tp4-drafter-1 (the default drafter manifest, dedf8df6: the control arm and the bf16 arm) and tp4-drafter-b16-1 (the block-16 candidate manifest, b16-98759a49). Both are built by the
# integration step from the same commit, the candidate with C2_DRAFTER_MANIFEST (B1); the candidate's fixtures are staged on the build host first (drafter_stage.py stage).
# A tag that already exists is skipped by the build step: the tags must be fresh. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# D-T2: the CANDIDATE tau arm b16-bf8: the block-16 fine-tune (0xBakeer/TandemLLM-Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-b16 at its pinned revision, Apache-2.0 with a LICENSE file; b32 is excluded: its licence is a
# metadata field only) on image tp4-drafter-b16-1, projection weights bfloat8_b as served. The lab refuses (exit 2, nothing sent) unless the container's own log shows '[DRAFTER_MANIFEST] b16-98759a49 in force'. No A3 (it is the
# control's calibration). Before pushing, ADD C2_TAULAB_PAIR_CONTROL=<the run id of D-T1> (digits; the job reader refuses this template without it): the step then runs drafter_pair_report.py against that run's rig-local results and prints the
# verdict line. Thinking ON, coding-agent turns from the public SWE-rebench set (A1) and the scrubbed own-session set (A2) as the lab already uses, no customer traffic; the data directory is rig-local and
# read-only to the job (kwork64/taulab/data under the runner's home), checked against its manifest before the container starts. The serving profile is c2-packed-tp4 with the lab's two
# arithmetic-neutral log flags and, for a drafter arm, only that arm's drafter-only flags. Judged PAIRED per turn id by drafter_pair_report.py against the control arm (the GO rule is in its
# docstring and docs/drafter-arms.md): pooled ratio lower 95%% bound > 1.00, no regression in the 80k+ bucket or at p10, identical text, both runs launched clean and asked the same questions; the control A3 verdict is an annotation. Duration (estimate): 85 min (the deadline of 80 min is counted from the container start, the load included). Kill rule: a launched-argv problem line (the manifest never named), a stall or a tripped breaker ends the arm.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset taulab
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-drafter-b16-1
C2_TAULAB_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_TAULAB_DRAFTER_ARM=b16-bf8
C2_TAULAB_ARMS=A1 A2
C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE=80
C2_TAULAB_IN_FLIGHT=8
